# Worker: Intake UX & Statute Selection

## Goal (Master-aligned)

Ship the IR-first desktop flow **Intake → Compare → Report**: complaint intake, multi-select WAC/RCW, Compare, stepper chrome, and App shell rails. Selection UX feeds approved codes into IR drafting — it does not author legal text.

## Role boundary

**Owns:** stepper labels/CTAs, Complaint/WAC/Review steps, statute search & related panels, selection state, desktop rails (drawers = small-breakpoint fallback), frontend API client wiring for those surfaces.

**Does not own:** allegation/quote/DOCX body (IR Drafting), PDF ingest/ranking (Corpus), case save/resume/status/export pack (Case Review), PII gate (Privacy), auth (Identity), launch config (DevEx).

## Invariants

- Primary path is Intake → Compare → Report; IR-primary wins over UX convenience
- Research / related-statute panels are **not authorization** — label and gate accordingly; only explicit user multi-select authorizes codes
- Never invent or paraphrase statute text in UI copy; show store-backed text or clear “unavailable / unverified” states
- Preserve desktop rail behavior; drawers remain fallback at smaller breakpoints
- User-facing copy is **investigator/application language only** — never show internal codes (`lexical_overlap`, `match_score`, `not_in_store`, prompt/model jargon). Use `investigatorLabels.ts`.

## Anti-goals

- Do not revive analyzer-first / dashboard-first UX as the default (trigger phrases, stats dashboards, generic findings lists)
- Do not treat search hits, related panels, or LLM suggestions as approved selections
- Do not invent statute quotes or subsection labels in copy, empty states, or placeholders
- Do not break zero-WAC / clear-selection affordances that keep the IR path honest
- Do not surface ranking reasons, scores, LLM model ids, or API field names in the UI

## Success criteria

- Step labels and CTAs stay aligned with Intake → Compare → Report
- Multi-select WAC/RCW and Compare states are clear; zero-WAC remains actionable
- Research panels are visually/verbally distinct from authorized selections
- Desktop rails work; no regression to analyzer-dashboard as the home path

## Escalation map

| Signal | Escalate to |
|--------|-------------|
| Allegation payload / quotes / IR sections | IR Drafting |
| Empty/wrong search or ranking results | Statute Corpus |
| Save/resume, review status, export pack | Case Review |
| Category 3/4 on complaint text | Privacy |
| Login / roles blocking the stepper | Identity Admin |
| Ports / Launch.bat / debug | Local DevEx |

Return the standard handoff block from `AGENTS.md`.
